rom one disk to another; it is about building a **resilience strategy**. A backup is only reliable if it can be verified, restored quickly, and protected from the same threats that destroyed the original data.\n\nHere is a detailed guide on designing a reliable file backup system.\n\n---\n\n### 1. Backup Strategies: Full vs. Incremental\nA hybrid approach is generally the most reliable and efficient.\n\n#### Full Backups\nA full backup copies every selected file and folder, regardless of whether they have changed.\n*   **Pros:** Simplest to restore;", "elapsed_s": 5.330154124996625, "ttft_s": 0.8852946879924275, "usage": {"completion_tokens": 128, "prompt_tokens": 54, "total_tokens": 182, "prompt_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 0}}, "timings": {"cache_n": 0, "prompt_n": 54, "prompt_ms": 551.097, "prompt_per_token_ms": 10.205499999999999, "prompt_per_second": 97.98637989319485, "predicted_n": 128, "predicted_ms": 4444.553, "predicted_per_token_ms": 34.99648031496063, "predicted_per_second": 28.574302072671877}, "finish_reason": "length", "decode_tps_client": 28.572332106321245, "end_to_end_output_tps": 24.014314970691593, "full_output_budget": true}, "measured": [{"text": "Designing a reliable file backup system is not merely about copying data from one drive to another; it is about building a **resilience strategy**. A backup is only reliable if it can be verified, restored quickly, and protected from the same threats that destroyed the original data.\n\nBelow is a comprehensive guide to designing a professional-grade backup system.\n\n---\n\n### 1. The Foundational Strategy: The 3-2-1 Rule\nBefore choosing tools, adhere to the industry standard for data redundancy:\n*   **3 Copies of Data:** One primary copy and two backups.\n*   **2 Different Media Types:** (e.g", "elapsed_s": 5.239766023994889, "ttft_s": 0.7941367999883369, "usage": {"completion_tokens": 128, "prompt_tokens": 55, "total_tokens": 183, "prompt_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 0}}, "timings": {